{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nEighteen Python modules under `tests/unit` contain 23 audited prose blocks, all true leading docstrings. Scope was revalidated against `origin/main@9e6a0e436520f67962c22dc244d7b4f77f5bee45`. The original numeric spans included imports and executable tails; those are removed. Current code now resolves the plan-review SHA through `gate_context`, validates compatible-provider config through `structured_run`, and enriches grades through `decide_ops`; this plan preserves those current seams.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the stable-ID blocks below. For every owned path, retain immutable before and final blobs and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies, remove only an allowlisted leading `Expr(Constant(str))` that is the first statement of a `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, or `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining normalized ASTs to match.\n\nTokenize both blobs and reject every changed inline comment or non-allowlisted full-line comment. Preserve non-docstring runtime strings, regexes, prompts, imports, decorators, annotations, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing physical lines exactly. Adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed only around an edited block.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_keygen_heldout.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_kind_vocabulary.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_local_verify_binding.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_own_pub_resolution_d26a.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_second_from_env_call_has_no_inline_key`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_public_counterpart_guard_879b.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_mint_warns_when_signed_key_pub_absent_though_another_chain_key_resolves`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_rollback_heldout.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py`: `D:test_shutdown_does_not_wait_for_an_in_flight_job`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_integrity_heldout.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_storage_heldout.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_storage.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_openai_compatible_provider.py` — 4 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_documented_local_server_recipe_returns_a_structured_verdict`\n  - `D:test_base_url_does_not_hijack_provider_selection`\n  - `D:test_per_class_endpoint_routes_the_primary_through_the_local_builder`\n- `tests/unit/test_openai_responses_contract.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_oracle_grade_split.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_output_schemas.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py`: `D:test_output_budget_scales_with_the_batchs_candidate_count`\n\n`D:<symbol>` is a true leading docstring. `C:<scope>:before:<code>` is one maximal full-line comment region anchored to unchanged code. No other prose is editable. In reviewer TSV, `stable_block_id` is the path-qualified `<path>#<D:...>` or `<path>#<C:...>` value.\n\n## Protected false positives\nAll unlisted docstrings/comments and every executable line incidentally covered by the old ranges are protected. In particular, short per-case AC docstrings outside this allowlist, inline fixture annotations, and all directives remain byte-exact.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\n- Op-cert prose keeps concurrency-safe key genesis, verify-never-creates, signed subject/payload authority, own-public-key resolution, consume-once private-key handling, specific-counterpart warnings, rollback-era judgment, service integrity, and storage/compaction behavior.\n- Service/producer prose keeps current DSSE producer, authentication, nonblocking warning, and structural shutdown contracts.\n- Provider prose keeps exact local endpoint configuration, provider-selection separation, per-class endpoint routing, Chat/Responses wire behavior, and retry scope.\n- Snapshot/schema/evaluation prose keeps immutable configuration, narrow public schemas, oracle-grade semantics, and batch-scaled overlap output.\n- All modules are direct pytest inputs. Mechanism-baseline entries source-identify the Responses/snapshot fixtures; migration, single-definition, and impact-plan tests reference the named suites. No target import, `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc consumer was found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only declared stable-ID blocks change.\n- [ ] Adjacent blank-line changes are limited to edited blocks.\n- [ ] The normalized-AST comparison passes on every owned path.\n- [ ] The token/comment comparison passes on every owned path.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter.\n- [ ] Every edited block retains its listed current contract.\n- [ ] Edited prose contains no chronology, duplication, obvious narration, or separator ornament.\n- [ ] An independent reviewer posts one leaf-linked TSV row per block with these columns: `stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\n- [ ] Before citations use `9e6a0e436520f67962c22dc244d7b4f77f5bee45:<path>#<stable-id>`.\n- [ ] Final citations use `<final-commit-sha>:<path>#<stable-id>`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `directives_exact=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `semantic-preservation=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n- [ ] All five structured verify commands pass.\n\n## Verification\nThe five DD-level commands recorded on this ticket run focused pytest (including real consumers), scoped Ruff check plus format-check, comment hygiene, owned-path `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify`. They are the executable completion oracle."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788661495019502001,"uuid":"8d28178e-f6f4-4e62-a210-df22d34f0e44"}